WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.440
All week long, we've been dishing

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.930
out tips and tricks to viewers like you

3
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.810
who may just love design or have a design dilemma.

4
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.460
And it is time for a very special design by Drew.

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.970
We heard from a husband and wife

6
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.360
who were looking for ways to transform their bedroom

7
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.900
in their forever home.

8
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.070
Oh, this is so fun.

9
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.650
Take a look.

10
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:22.820 line:15%
I'm Lily.

11
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.200 line:15%
This is my husband, Zach.

12
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.893
We met on set at work.

13
00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:28.470
I do hair styling for film and TV

14
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.960
and do the special effects.

15
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.980 line:15%
Little did we know it slowed down for the whole world,

16
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.950
and we were out of a job.

17
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.810
Yep.

18
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.070
The pandemic changed everything.

19
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.310
When we had to pull out of our mortgage,

20
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.500
his parents decided they needed to sell his childhood home.

21
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.700
It opened up the doors

22
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.570
and we decided to relocate north of the city.

23
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.563
The house has been updated probably

24
00:00:49.563 --> 00:00:51.910
in a little over 40 years.

25
00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.930
There was nothing that Lily really thoroughly liked

26
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.763
about the house.

27
00:00:55.763 --> 00:00:57.000
Other than where it was.

28
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.080
We ended up tearing out most of the house

29
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.032
and made it more suitable for our taste

30
00:01:02.032 --> 00:01:02.865
and our interest.

31
00:01:02.865 --> 00:01:04.320
What we needed and stuff.

32
00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.020
We had our first born Oliver, who's amazing.

33
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.230
We had a lot of catching up to do once he was born.

34
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.160
And that's kind of where all our focus has been

35
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.900
on the last, what year and a half.

36
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.920
His nursery is like the only room that's been complete.

37
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.300
Our master has nothing, but a broken bed.

38
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.880
He gets in bed, I just like slowly roll over to his side.

39
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.030
'Cause it's a broken lop-sided bed.

40
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.343
But that's what we've had for over a year.

41
00:01:29.343 --> 00:01:30.176
It works.

42
00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:31.750
But Oliver has his room set up

43
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.040
and he's happy and that's what matters.

44
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.540
But would be really nice to have just a alone time together.

45
00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.590
Please help us with our master bedroom.

46
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.860
We could really use peace and quiet and tranquility.

47
00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.575
Please help us get our space back.

48
00:01:44.575 --> 00:01:46.743
(audience clapping)

49
00:01:46.743 --> 00:01:51.415
Please welcome Lily and Zach Maggio.

50
00:01:51.415 --> 00:01:52.248
Hi guys.

51
00:01:52.248 --> 00:01:53.602
I'm already crying.

52
00:01:53.602 --> 00:01:56.801
Oh yes, oh the hormones must be raging.

53
00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:57.693
Totally.

54
00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.060
I love Zach,

55
00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.970
I mean the childhood home.

56
00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:03.803
Yeah.

57
00:02:03.803 --> 00:02:04.940
Tell me about this.

58
00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.040
It's awesome.

59
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.040 line:15%
So I grew up there.

60
00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.420 line:15%
I had an older brother and older sister.

61
00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.253 line:15%
Growing up there,

62
00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:13.161 line:15%
I never realized how special it was.

63
00:02:13.161 --> 00:02:15.240
Now living there each day

64
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.240
I get to see my son have the same memories that kinda I had.

65
00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.110
And then a couple, probably about six months ago,

66
00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.750
it really dawned on me when my sister,

67
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.120
yeah, my sister, my mother, and my sister's son

68
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.300
were running through the backyard

69
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.210
and my mom was chasing both of them.

70
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.150
So that was something special to me.

71
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.250
Oh my God.

72
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.600
I'm just so glad that your kids

73
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.443
are getting this opportunity.

74
00:02:39.443 --> 00:02:40.710
Yeah.

75
00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.143
It's really amazing.

76
00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.950
Why haven't you had time to focus on the bedroom?

77
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.930
I feel like the answer is obvious.

78
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.780 line:15%
Well with COVID, not having a job for a year.

79
00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:54.613 line:15%
Right?

80
00:02:54.613 --> 00:02:56.810
And then his ankle, he hurt his ankle that year.

81
00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:00.793
And then I, we got so lucky.

82
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.800
It was so quick.

83
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.890
So yeah, so we just haven't had a chance.

84
00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.734
I don't even know how our bedroom encouraged this.

85
00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.044
(audience laughing)

86
00:03:12.044 --> 00:03:12.877
But it did.

87
00:03:12.877 --> 00:03:14.817
(audience clapping)

88
00:03:14.817 --> 00:03:17.240
Well, if it's okay,

89
00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.300
I looked at the before pictures of your bedroom.

90
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.133
Yes.

91
00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.693
And I got really inspired.

92
00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.940
Very excited.

93
00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.540
Okay, I really got into it.

94
00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.750
I got really inspired

95
00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.966
